{"variant": "U2_expl_fmt", "id": "exlog_expand_exp_sub_recover", "repeat": 0, "tier": "hard", "field": "exp-log", "language": "en", "outcome": "answered", "reason": null, "kind": "prove", "answer": null, "tactic": "model_0", "tactic_text": "intro x y\nrw [← Real.exp_add]\nring", "verified": true, "formal": "∀ x y : ℝ, Real.exp (x - y) * Real.exp y = Real.exp x", "proved": "∀ x y : ℝ, Real.exp (x - y) * Real.exp y = Real.exp x", "explanation": "Let $x$ and $y$ be real numbers. The key idea is to combine the two exponential factors using the rule that a product of exponentials is the exponential of the sum.\n\nBy the exponential addition law, $\\exp(x-y)\\exp(y)=\\exp((x-y)+y)$.\n\nThe exponent simplifies because $(x-y)+y=x$, so $\\exp((x-y)+y)=\\exp(x)$.\n\nTherefore, for all real $x$ and $y$, $\\exp(x-y)\\exp(y)=\\exp(x)$.", "request": "For all real x and y, exp(x - y)*exp(y) = exp(x).", "seconds": {"first_call": 2.148, "closed": 2.49, "verified": 2.957, "gate": 4.081, "explained": 5.258, "explanation_review": 2.224, "reviewed": 7.482, "total": 7.482}, "explanation_approved": true, "explanation_issue": "", "item_usd": 0.000695, "statements": ["∀ x y : ℝ, Real.exp (x - y) * Real.exp y = Real.exp x"], "gate": {"passed": true, "reasons": [], "agree": true, "reviewed": true, "roundtrip": true, "issue": "", "rt_issue": ""}, "calls": [{"label": "merged", "model": "gpt-6-luna", "effort": "none", "prompt_chars": 1355, "input_tokens": 436, "output_tokens": 66, "start": 0.0, "end": 2.148, "seconds": 2.147, "error": null}, {"label": "merged", "model": "gpt-6-luna", "effort": "none", "prompt_chars": 1355, "input_tokens": 436, "output_tokens": 71, "start": 0.001, "end": 2.783, "seconds": 2.783, "error": null}, {"label": "merged", "model": "gpt-6-luna", "effort": "none", "prompt_chars": 1355, "input_tokens": 436, "output_tokens": 85, "start": 0.0, "end": 2.886, "seconds": 2.885, "error": null}, {"label": "review_terse", "model": "gpt-6-luna", "effort": "none", "prompt_chars": 852