{"variant": "U2_expl_fmt", "id": "logic_add_neq_contrapositive_real", "repeat": 0, "tier": "hard", "field": "discrete-logic", "language": "en", "outcome": "answered", "reason": null, "kind": "prove", "answer": null, "tactic": "model_0", "tactic_text": "intro x y z h heq\napply h\nrw [heq]", "verified": true, "formal": "∀ x y z : ℝ, x + z ≠ y + z → x ≠ y", "proved": "∀ x y z : ℝ, x + z ≠ y + z → x ≠ y", "explanation": "Let $x$, $y$, and $z$ be real numbers. The proof uses the fact that if $x=y$, then adding the same number $z$ to both sides gives equal sums.\n\nAssume $x+z\\neq y+z$. To prove $x\\neq y$, suppose instead that $x=y$.\n\nReplacing $y$ with $x$ in $y+z$ then gives $y+z=x+z$, so the two sums are equal. This contradicts the assumption that $x+z\\neq y+z$. Thus $x$ cannot equal $y$.\n\nTherefore, for all real $x$, $y$, and $z$, if $x+z\\neq y+z$, then $x\\neq y$.", "request": "For all real x, y, and z, if x + z ≠ y + z then x ≠ y.", "seconds": {"first_call": 2.319, "closed": 2.712, "verified": 3.128, "gate": 4.966, "explained": 5.919, "explanation_review": 3.013, "reviewed": 8.932, "total": 8.932}, "explanation_approved": true, "explanation_issue": "", "item_usd": 0.000764, "statements": ["∀ x y z : ℝ, x + z ≠ y + z → x ≠ y"], "gate": {"passed": true, "reasons": [], "agree": true, "reviewed": true, "roundtrip": true, "issue": "", "rt_issue": ""}, "calls": [{"label": "merged", "model": "gpt-6-luna", "effort": "none", "prompt_chars": 1360, "input_tokens": 442, "output_tokens": 68, "start": 0.002, "end": 2.319, "seconds": 2.317, "error": null}, {"label": "merged", "model": "gpt-6-luna", "effort": "none", "prompt_chars": 1360, "input_tokens": 442, "output_tokens": 113, "start": 0.0, "end": 2.719, "seconds": 2.719, "error": null}, {"label": "merged", "model": "gpt-6-luna", "effort": "none", "prompt_chars": 1360, "input_tokens": 442, "output_tokens": 114, "start": 0.0, "end": 2.858, "seconds": 2.858, "error": null}, {"label": "review_terse", "model": "gpt-6-luna"