{"variant": "U2_expl_fmt", "id": "pq-real-sequence-limit-uniqueness", "repeat": 0, "tier": "medium", "field": "calculus-analysis", "language": "ja", "outcome": "fallthrough", "reason": "no_candidate_closed", "kind": "explain", "answer": null, "tactic": null, "tactic_text": null, "verified": false, "formal": null, "proved": null, "explanation": null, "request": "実数列(u_n)が実数aとbの両方に収束するとき、a=bであることをε–N論法で証明してください。aへの収束とは、任意のε>0に対してあるN∈ℕが存在し、n≥Nなら|u_n−a|<εとなることです。bへの収束も同じ意味とします。", "seconds": {"first_call": 1.976, "total": 9.457}, "explanation_approved": null, "explanation_issue": "", "item_usd": 0.001017, "statements": [], "gate": null, "calls": [{"label": "merged", "model": "gpt-6-luna", "effort": "none", "prompt_chars": 1420, "input_tokens": 508, "output_tokens": 30, "start": 0.0, "end": 1.976, "seconds": 1.975, "error": null}, {"label": "merged", "model": "gpt-6-luna", "effort": "none", "prompt_chars": 1420, "input_tokens": 508, "output_tokens": 675, "start": 0.001, "end": 6.569, "seconds": 6.568, "error": null}, {"label": "merged", "model": "gpt-6-luna", "effort": "none", "prompt_chars": 1420, "input_tokens": 508, "output_tokens": 820, "start": 0.0, "end": 8.479, "seconds": 8.479, "error": null}, {"label": "review_terse", "model": "gpt-6-luna", "effort": "none", "prompt_chars": 1016, "input_tokens": 392, "output_tokens": 22, "start": 6.57, "end": 8.622, "seconds": 2.052, "error": null}, {"label": "review_terse", "model": "gpt-6-luna", "effort": "none", "prompt_chars": 1076, "input_tokens": 404, "output_tokens": 22, "start": 6.57, "end": 8.685, "seconds": 2.115, "error": null}]}
{"variant": "U2_expl_fmt", "id": "rat_adjacent_partial_fractions", "repeat": 0, "tier": "hard", "field": "school-algebra", "language": "en", "outcome": "answered", "reason": null, "kind": "prove", "answer": null, "tactic": "grind", "tactic_text": "intros; grind", "verified": true, "formal": "∀ x : ℝ, x ≠ -1 → x ≠ -2 → (2 * x + 3) / ((x + 1) * (x + 2)) = 1 / (x + 1) + 1 / (x + 2)", "proved": "∀ x : ℝ, x ≠ -1 → x ≠ -2 → (2 * x + 3) / ((x + 1) * (x + 2)) = 1 / (x + 1) + 1 / (x + 2)", "explanation": "Let $x$ be real and assume $x\\neq -1$ and $x\\neq -2$. The identity follows by combining the two fractions over a common denominator.\n\nBecause $x\\neq -1$, we have $x+1\\neq 0$, and because $x\\neq -2$, we have $x+2\\neq 0$. Thus the common denominator $(x+1)(x+2)$ is nonzero, so the right-hand side can be combined over it.\n\nPutting the fractions over this denominator gives numerator $(x+2)+(x+1)=2x+3$. Hence the right-hand side is $(2x+3)/((x+1)(x+2))$, as claimed.\n\nTherefore the stated identity holds for every real $x$ with $x\\neq -1$ and $x\\neq -2$.", "request": "For every real x with x ≠ -1 and x ≠ -2, (2x+3)/((x+1)(x+2)) = 1/(x+1) + 1/(x+2).", "seconds": {"first_call": 2.479, "closed": 3.265, "verified": 3.883, "gate": 4.603, "explained": 6.63, "explanation_review": 3.139, "reviewed": 9.769, "total": 9.769}, "explanation_approved": true, "explanation_issue": "", "item_usd": 0.000842, "statements": ["∀ x : ℝ, x ≠ -1 → x ≠ -2 → (2 * x + 3) / ((x + 1) * (x + 2)) = 1 / (x + 1) + 1 / (x + 2)"], "gate": {"passed": true, "reasons": [], "agree": true, "reviewed": true, "roundtrip": true, "issue": "", "rt_issue": ""}, "calls": [{"label": "merged", "model": "gpt-6-luna", "effort": "none", "prompt_chars": 1387, "input_tokens": 465, "output_tokens": 106, "start": 0.001, "end": 2.479, "seconds": 2.479, "error": null}, {"label": "merged", "model": "gpt-6-luna", "effort": "none", "prompt_chars": 1387, "input_tokens": 465, "output_tokens": 103, "start": 0.001, "end": 2.706, "